  "output": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Three open decisions — positions needed from Priya and Sam</title>\n<style>\n  :root {\n    --ink: #1a1a1a;\n    --muted: #5c5c5c;\n    --rule: #d8d4cc;\n    --paper: #fbfaf7;\n    --panel: #fff;\n    --accent: #8a4b1f;\n    --open: #a33c1c;\n  }\n  * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n  body {\n    margin: 0;\n    background: var(--paper);\n    color: var(--ink);\n    font: 16px/1.6 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, \"Helvetica Neue\", Arial, sans-serif;\n  }\n  .wrap { max-width: 52rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 1.5rem 6rem; }\n  header { border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink); padding-bottom: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }\n  h1 { font-size: 1.9rem; line-height: 1.25; margin: 0 0 .5rem; letter-spacing: -.01em; }\n  .sub { color: var(--muted); margin: 0; }\n  h2 {\n    font-size: 1.3rem; margin: 3rem 0 .75rem; letter-spacing: -.01em;\n    padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);\n  }\n  h3 { font-size: 1rem; margin: 1.75rem 0 .5rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; color: var(--muted); }\n  p { margin: 0 0 1rem; }\n  .tag {\n    display: inline-block; font: 700 .7rem/1 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;\n    letter-spacing: .12em; color: #fff; background: var(--open);\n    padding: .35rem .5rem; border-radius: 3px; vertical-align: .18em; margin-right: .5rem;\n  }\n  blockquote {\n    margin: 1.25rem 0; padding: .75rem 0 .75rem 1.25rem;\n    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); color: var(--muted);\n  }\n  pre {\n    background: #f2efe9; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 4px;\n    padding: .85rem 1rem; overflow-x: auto;\n    font: .85rem/1.5 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;\n  }\n  code { font: .9em ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; background: #f2efe9; padding: .1em .3em; border-radius: 3px; }\n  pre code { background: none; padding: 0; }\n  .stakes {\n    background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-left: 3px solid var(--ink);\n    padding: 1rem 1.25rem; margin: 1.5rem 0;\n  }\n  .stakes strong { display: block; font-size: .78rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .1em; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: .35rem; }\n  .stakes p { margin: 0; }\n\n  form { margin-top: 1rem; }\n  fieldset {\n    border: 1px solid var(--rule); background: var(--panel);\n    border-radius: 5px; padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem 1.5rem; margin: 1.25rem 0 0;\n  }\n  legend { font-weight: 700; padding: 0 .5rem; font-size: .95rem; }\n  .q { margin-bottom: 1.4rem; }\n  .q:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }\n  .qlabel { font-weight: 600; display: block; margin-bottom: .6rem; }\n  label.opt {\n    display: flex; gap: .6rem; align-items: flex-start;\n    padding: .4rem .5rem; border-radius: 4px; cursor: pointer;\n  }\n  label.opt:hover { background: #f4f1ea; }\n  label.opt input { margin-top: .35rem; flex: none; }\n  textarea, input[type=text] {\n    width: 100%; font: inherit; font-size: .95rem; color: var(--ink);\n    border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 4px; padding: .6rem .7rem;\n    background: #fffefb; resize: vertical;\n  }\n  textarea:focus, input:focus { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: -1px; }\n  .why { margin-top: .6rem; }\n  .why span { display: block; font-size: .82rem; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: .3rem; }\n  .actions { margin-top: 2rem; display: flex; gap: .75rem; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; }\n  button {\n    font: 600 .95rem/1 inherit; padding: .75rem 1.1rem; border-radius: 4px;\n    border: 1px solid var(--ink); background: var(--ink); color: #fff; cursor: pointer;\n  }\n  button.ghost { background: transparent; color: var(--ink); }\n  button:hover { opacity: .85; }\n  #out { margin-top: 1.25rem; }\n  #out textarea { min-height: 22rem; font: .82rem/1.5 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; }\n  .note { font-size: .85rem; color: var(--muted); }\n  ul { margin: 0 0 1rem; padding-left: 1.2rem; }\n  li { margin-bottom: .35rem; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"wrap\">\n\n<header>\n  <h1>Three open decisions in <code>docs/DESIGN.md</code></h1>\n  <p class=\"sub\">The argument as it currently stands, and a position needed from each of Priya and Sam on all three.</p>\n</header>\n\n<p>Three items in the design doc are marked <code>OPEN</code>. They are not independent: the first one decides whether the service is worth building at all, the second decides who is allowed to receive a link, and the third decides what agents actually touch. Below is the case as written, then the form.</p>\n\n<h2><span class=\"tag\">OPEN 1</span>The core bet: a schema, not a framework</h2>\n\n<p>The claim: generating bespoke HTML costs thousands of output tokens every time, and that generation — not context loading, not deploy latency — is where the current approach is slow and expensive. So the agent-facing surface is a <strong>schema it emits against</strong>, not a framework it programs against:</p>\n\n<pre><code>{\"type\": \"decision-matrix\", \"options\": [...], \"criteria\": [...]}</code></pre>\n\n<p>That is claimed as a 20–50× token reduction over an authored page, and it is the entire reason this service exists. Any design decision that pushes agents back toward writing markup has broken the bet.</p>\n\n<blockquote>Worth confirming against two or three real past generations before committing. If the dominant cost turns out to be context loading rather than generation, the answer is a cached design doc, not this service.</blockquote>\n\n<div class=\"stakes\">\n  <strong>What's at stake</strong>\n  <p>This is the load-bearing assumption. If generation is not the dominant cost, the correct build is a cached design doc and the rest of the doc is moot. The measurement is cheap; the question is whether it blocks further work or runs alongside it.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"tag\">OPEN 2</span>The per-dev cluster problem</h2>\n\n<p>Every dev runs their own independent single-node k3s cluster behind their own tunnel. So a participant link points at <em>that dev's box</em>. A stakeholder clicking it six hours later gets an answer only if that box is still up — and the box is also a NixOS host that gets rebuilt.</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>For a dev-phase tool this is probably tolerable: the boxes are always-on and the blast radius is one dev's briefs.</li>\n  <li>It is <em>not</em> tolerable if links go to people outside the team. A dead link to an external stakeholder is worse than never having sent one.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>The cheap insurance, taken now: <strong>never bake the host into a brief's identity.</strong> A handle and a participant token identify a brief; the hostname serving it is deployment configuration. That costs nothing today and keeps \"move it to one shared deployment\" a config change rather than a migration.</p>\n\n<div class=\"stakes\">\n  <strong>What's at stake</strong>\n  <p>The insurance is already taken. The open question is whether host-agnostic identity is <em>sufficient</em> for now, or whether external-facing links need an actual policy or guardrail before someone sends one.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"tag\">OPEN 3</span>Agent-facing interface: MCP over the top?</h2>\n\n<p>The REST API is built — see <code>README.md</code> for the routes. It is bearer-authenticated and is what the participant-facing app uses too.</p>\n\n<p>Proposed: an MCP server over the top, exposing <code>list_widgets</code>, <code>create_brief</code>, <code>await_responses</code> as tools. That is the idiomatic agent-facing surface and would remove the need for an agent to remember curl invocations. REST stays underneath either way, because an orchestrator resuming a session is not necessarily an agent.</p>\n\n<div class=\"stakes\">\n  <strong>What's at stake</strong>\n  <p>Not whether REST survives — it does. Whether MCP is built now, deferred until REST friction is demonstrated, or dropped in favour of documentation.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h2>Positions</h2>\n<p class=\"note\">Fill in your own section. Nothing is sent anywhere — use the button at the bottom to produce a plain-text summary you can paste back into the thread or the doc.</p>\n\n<form id=\"f\">\n\n  <fieldset>\n    <legend>Priya</legend>\n\n    <div class=\"q\">\n      <span class=\"qlabel\">1. The core bet — validate before committing?</span>\n      <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"p1\" value=\"Audit 2–3 real past generations before any further build\"><span>Audit 2–3 real past generations <em>before</em> any further build</span></label>\n      <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"p1\" value=\"Proceed on the bet; run the audit in parallel\"><span>Proceed on the bet; run the audit in parallel</span></label>\n      <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"p1\" value=\"Bet is already settled; no audit needed\"><span>Bet is already settled; no audit needed</span></label>\n      <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"p1\" value=\"Reject the framing (see reasoning)\"><span>Reject the framing — the cost question is posed wrong</span></label>\n      <label class=\"why\"><span>Why — and if you want the audit, what result would change your mind?</span><textarea name=\"p1why\" rows=\"3\"></textarea></label>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"q\">\n      <span class=\"qlabel\">2. Per-dev cluster / link durability</span>\n      <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"p2\" value=\"Host-agnostic identity is enough for now; ship\"><span>Host-agnostic identity is enough for now; ship</span></label>\n      <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"p2\" value=\"Enough, plus an explicit internal-only policy on participant links\"><span>Enough, <em>plus</em> an explicit internal-only policy on participant links</span></label>\n      <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"p2\" value=\"Need a technical guardrail before any external link is possible\"><span>Need a technical guardrail before any external link is possible</span></label>\n      <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"p2\" value=\"Move to one shared deployment now\"><span>Move to one shared deployment now</span></label>\n      <label class=\"why\"><span>Why — and what would trigger the move to shared deployment?</span><textarea name=\"p2why\" rows=\"3\"></textarea></label>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"q\">\n      <span class=\"qlabel\">3. MCP server over the REST API</span>\n      <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"p3\" value=\"Build MCP now\"><span>Build it now — it's the idiomatic surface</span></label>\n      <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"p3\" value=\"Defer until REST friction is demonstrated\"><span>Defer until REST friction is actually demonstrated</span></label>\n      <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"p3\" value=\"Don't build; REST plus good docs is enough\"><span>Don't build it; REST plus good docs is enough</span></label>\n      <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"p3\" value=\"Other (see reasoning)\"><span>Other</span></label>\n      <label class=\"why\"><span>Why — and which of the three tools, if any, is the one that matters?</span><textarea name=\"p3why\" rows=\"3\"></textarea></label>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"q\">\n      <label class=\"why\"><span>Anything else — including any open item you think is missing</span><textarea name=\"pextra\" rows=\"3\"></textarea></label>\n    </div>\n  </fieldset>\n\n  <fieldset>\n    <legend>Sam</legend>\n\n    <div class=\"q\">\n      <span class=\"qlabel\">1. The core bet — validate before committing?</span>\n      <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"s1\" value=\"Audit 2–3 real past generations before any further build\"><span>Audit 2–3 real past generations <em>before</em> any further build</span></label>\n      <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"s1\" value=\"Proceed on the bet; run the audit in parallel\"><span>Proceed on the bet; run the audit in parallel</span></label>\n      <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"s1\" value=\"Bet is already settled; no audit needed\"><span>Bet is already settled; no audit needed</span></label>\n      <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"s1\" value=\"Reject the framing (see reasoning)\"><span>Reject the framing — the cost question is posed wrong</span></label>\n      <label class=\"why\"><span>Why — and if you want the audit, what result would change your mind?</span><textarea name=\"s1why\" rows=\"3\"></textarea></label>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"q\">\n      <span class=\"qlabel\">2. Per-dev cluster / link durability</span>\n      <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"s2\" value=\"Host-agnostic identity is enough for now; ship\"><span>Host-agnostic identity is enough for now; ship</span></label>\n      <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"s2\" value=\"Enough, plus an explicit internal-only policy on participant links\"><span>Enough, <em>plus</em> an explicit internal-only policy on participant links</span></label>\n      <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"s2\" value=\"Need a technical guardrail before any external link is possible\"><span>Need a technical guardrail before any external link is possible</span></label>\n      <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"s2\" value=\"Move to one shared deployment now\"><span>Move to one shared deployment now</span></label>\n      <label class=\"why\"><span>Why — and what would trigger the move to shared deployment?</span><textarea name=\"s2why\" rows=\"3\"></textarea></label>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"q\">\n      <span class=\"qlabel\">3. MCP server over the REST API</span>\n      <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"s3\" value=\"Build MCP now\"><span>Build it now — it's the idiomatic surface</span></label>\n      <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"s3\" value=\"Defer until REST friction is demonstrated\"><span>Defer until REST friction is actually demonstrated</span></label>\n      <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"s3\" value=\"Don't build; REST plus good docs is enough\"><span>Don't build it; REST plus good docs is enough</span></label>\n      <label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"s3\" value=\"Other (see reasoning)\"><span>Other</span></label>\n      <label class=\"why\"><span>Why — and which of the three tools, if any, is the one that matters?</span><textarea name=\"s3why\" rows=\"3\"></textarea></label>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"q\">\n      <label class=\"why\"><span>Anything else — including any open item you think is missing</span><textarea name=\"sextra\" rows=\"3\"></textarea></label>\n    </div>\n  </fieldset>\n\n  <div class=\"actions\">\n    <button type=\"button\" id=\"gen\">Generate summary</button>\n    <button type=\"button\" class=\"ghost\" id=\"copy\">Copy to clipboard</button>\n    <button type=\"button\" class=\"ghost\" id=\"clear\">Clear form</button>\n  </div>\n  <div id=\"out\" hidden>\n    <textarea id=\"outtext\" readonly aria-label=\"Generated summary\"></textarea>\n  </div>\n</form>\n\n</div>\n\n<script>\n(function () {\n  var f = document.getElementById('f');\n  var out = document.getElementById('out');\n  var outtext = document.getElementById('outtext');\n\n  var items = [\n    ['1. Core bet: validate the token-cost assumption?', '1', '1why'],\n    ['2. Per-dev cluster / link durability', '2', '2why'],\n    ['3. MCP server over REST', '3', '3why']\n  ];\n\n  function val(name) {\n    var el = f.elements[name];\n    if (!el) return '';\n    if (el.length !== undefined && el[0] && el[0].type === 'radio') {\n      for (var i = 0; i < el.length; i++) if (el[i].checked) return el[i].value;\n      return '';\n    }\n    return (el.value || '').trim();\n  }\n\n  function person(label, prefix) {\n    var lines = ['## ' + label, ''];\n    items.forEach(function (it) {\n      var pos = val(prefix + it[1]) || '(no position given)';\n      var why = val(prefix + it[2]) || '(no reasoning given)';\n      lines.push('### ' + it[0]);\n      lines.push('Position: ' + pos);\n      lines.push('Why: ' + why);\n      lines.push('');\n    });\n    var extra = val(prefix + 'extra');\n    if (extra) { lines.push('### Other'); lines.push(extra); lines.push(''); }\n    return lines.join('\\n');\n  }\n\n  document.getElementById('gen').addEventListener('click', function () {\n    var text = '# Positions on the three OPEN items in docs/DESIGN.md\\n\\n'\n      + person('Priya', 'p') + '\\n' + person('Sam', 's');\n    outtext.value = text.replace(/\\n{3,}/g, '\\n\\n').trim() + '\\n';\n    out.hidden = false;\n    outtext.focus();\n    outtext.setSelectionRange(0, 0);\n  });\n\n  document.getElementById('copy').addEventListener('click', function () {\n    if (out.hidden) document.getElementById('gen').click();\n    outtext.select();\n    try { document.execCommand('copy'); } catch (e) {}\n    if (navigator.clipboard) navigator.clipboard.writeText(outtext.value).catch(function () {});\n    this.textContent = 'Copied';\n    var b = this;\n    setTimeout(function () { b.textContent = 'Copy to clipboard'; }, 1600);\n  });\n\n  document.getElementById('clear').addEventListener('click', function () {\n    if (confirm('Clear all answers?')) { f.reset(); out.hidden = true; outtext.value = ''; }\n  });\n})();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>"
